## AC-BASE-06 — spine entry point baseline
$ spine --help
spine — turn brief.md + script.md into the timed spine every plate hangs on

Usage: spine [options]

Reads the brief's runtime and beat list, and script.md (one "## <beat-id>" section per beat,
one paragraph each). With narration it synthesizes one clip per beat, lays them out with
--lead-ms/--tail-ms of silence inside each beat (so beats are separated by at least 400 ms),
and writes spine/narration.wav + spine/manifest.json. Without narration (--no-narrate, or no
PEAK_MEDIA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY (or legacy TTS_OPENROUTER_API_KEY) for a real model) it writes spine/beatgrid.json and a silent spine/narration.wav, with
no network calls. Narration is on by default when PEAK_MEDIA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY is set or --tts-model is fake/tone.
Exit 1 (files still written) when the runtime is outside the target ±10%: resize script.md.

Options:
      --brief <file>          The video brief (runtime and beat list) (default: brief.md)
      --script <file>         Narration script (default: script.md next to the brief)
      --out <dir>             Spine folder (default: spine/ next to the brief)
      --target-ms <ms>        Target runtime (overrides the brief)
      --narrate               Require narration (fails without PEAK_MEDIA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY unless --tts-model fake/tone)
      --no-narrate            Write a beat grid (no voice, no network)
      --tts-model <model>     TTS model (fake/tone for offline tests) (default: google/gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts)
      --voice <name>          TTS voice (default: Achird)
      --style <text>          Style instructions sent with every clip (default: )
      --lead-ms <ms>          Silence before the clip inside each beat (≥ 200) (default: 250)
      --tail-ms <ms>          Silence after the clip inside each beat (≥ 200) (default: 250)
      --max-hold-ms <ms>      Most extra hold added per beat when the spine runs short of the target (default: 1000)
      --bpm <n>               Beat-grid tempo; beat lengths snap to whole beats (default: 120)
      --audio-offset-ms <ms>  Recorded in the manifest for laying narration onto picture (default: 0)
      --cache-dir <dir>       TTS clip cache (default: ~/.cache/peak-media/tts)
      --export-clips <dir>    Copy every clip here (default: <out>/clips)
      --debug-requests        Log TTS requests (key redacted)
      --budget                Print the word budget per beat and exit (no synthesis, no network)
      --wpm <n>               Speaking rate for --budget (measure yours with sample-voice) (default: 165)
  -h, --help                  Show this help and exit
      --version               Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  spine --brief brief.md --budget
  spine --brief brief.md --tts-model fake/tone
  spine --brief brief.md --voice Achird --style "Clear, friendly explainer tone."
  spine --brief brief.md --no-narrate
exit=0
